{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_upwind_D1x_extrapolate_bc",
    "description": "Per-axis quantity diff2x of NCAR fire_behavior's classical Godunov level-set option (fire_upwinding = 4) on cartesian_uniform_2d with the linear-extrapolation halo closure, from which fire_behavior builds the front normal nvx = diff2x/sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps) while taking |grad psi| itself from the Rouy-Tourin Hamiltonian (rules/godunov_norm_D2_*). Match D(u, wrt: x) at priority 10, scoped with where {u: {shape: [x, y]}}. THE SCHEME, as Calc_tend_ls computes it: within bdy_eno1_cells of ANY wall (either axis) the ENO1 minmod of the two one-sided differences (fire_behavior's BDY_ENO1 band, whose test precedes the `select case (fire_upwinding)` and so overrides case (4)), and the Godunov-upwind quantity max(D-_x u, 0) - min(D+_x u, 0) everywhere else. Three regions -- the interior [2, NX-1] x [1, NY] is a single apply of stencils/godunov_upwind_D1x_interior (the per-cell wall-band switch, stencils/godunov_eno1_D1); the two wall lines i=1 and i=NX lie in the band for every bdy_eno1_cells >= 1 and are ENO1-only (stencils/eno1_minmod), with the out-of-range neighbour replaced by the guarded linear-extrapolation ghost. BOUNDARY CLOSURE bc:extrapolate_linear: the walls carry no prescribed value; instead each wall cell sees a one-cell halo ghost extrapolated from the two innermost cells, u[0,j] = max(2 u[1,j] - u[2,j], u[1,j], u[2,j]) (and symmetrically u[NX+1,j], u[i,0], u[i,NY+1]) -- stencils/extrapolate_linear_ghost, fire_behavior's Extrapol_var_at_bdys (HALO = 1, BIAS = 1). Only the three-point ENO1 stencil is evaluated at a wall cell, so one ghost suffices, as in the reference code. SIGN CAVEAT (fire_behavior note N44): for a field decreasing along x the Godunov branch returns -D+ > 0, a magnitude, while the ENO1 branch in the wall band returns the signed (negative) derivative -- the reference code's own inconsistency, reproduced; a consumer building a signed normal must carry the sign separately. EXACTNESS: on a linear field with positive slope along x the result is the slope on every cell EXCEPT the i=1 wall, where the field decreases toward the wall, the guard clamps the ghost to the neighbour (u[0] = u[2]), and the ENO1 minmod of D- = -slope, D+ = +slope is 0; first order otherwise. FREE NAMES (consumer-supplied, resolved in the consuming model's scope like the grid geometry dx): bdy_eno1_cells, the ENO1 wall band in cells (>= 1; fire_behavior's BDY_ENO1 = 10). Requires NX >= 3.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "axes:x,y",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:3",
      "bc:extrapolate_linear",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Osher, S., & Sethian, J. A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed: Algorithms based on Hamilton-Jacobi formulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 79(1), 12-49.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
